  "body": "Found another inconsistency between Synapse and the spec while working on ruma-client. Synapse sends events like this:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n    \"content\": {\r\n        \"currently_active\": true,\r\n        \"last_active_ago\": 66841020,\r\n        \"presence\": \"online\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"type\": \"m.presence\",\r\n    \"sender\": \"@someuser:matrix.org\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhere the user ID is in the sender field. According to the spec however, this information should be in the `user_id` field inside the events content: https://matrix.org/docs/spec/client_server/r0.2.0.html#m-presence\r\n(both in r0.2.0 and HEAD)",
